This was my first tourney.  I ended up with high score for healer,
Hat Trick, double top, and birdie with bells on.

In my first game, as a human wizard, I made it all the way down to the bottom,
and was on my way back up with the amulet.  In Orcus town, apparently I overlooked
killing Orcus on the way down (oops).  Orcus summoned Yeenoghu, and the two
of them summoned Demogorgon.  Ack.  Between the three of them, I ended up
dying of illness.  This was the first time I've ever died after reaching the
castle, not an auspicious start.

After ascending a neutral human male wizard, I next went for a lawful female
dwarven valk.  An early "death by falling rock trap" killed the "with bells on."
Other than that, nothing particularly eventful to report.

That left a chaotic character.  Oddly enough, I've never played chaotic, never
played an elf, and never played a priest, so that was my next choice :)  I managed
to ascend on my first try, so that gave me a double top and a birdie with bells
on.  Having automatic divination of blessed/uncursed/cursed status was pretty
nice.

Next up was a neutral female gnomish healer.  I'd never played a healer before
either.  This was also my first try at the protection racket, which took
me a few tries.  After I succeeded, it struck me as "much ado about nothing."
OK, so I got my 10 points of protection as a level 1 character, but so what?
A little patience and I almost always get there any way, so why risk being
too deep with an under prepared character?  YMMV.

The last character was a chaotic Orcish Barbarian.  First time playing an
Orc, and first time playing a barbarian (I already mentioned I've never
played chaotic before, so this should be no surprise).  Here, disaster
struck.  I got all the way to the bottom, found the vibrating square,
and was just about to start on my ascension run when the dungeon collapsed
on scheherazade.  My game was gone, with three days left.  I contacted
Robin, by there was no record of my barbarian at all.  Sigh.  Then, with
two days left, I decided to bite the bullet and try again.  This time,
I got down to the Valley of the Dead, and my game crashed again.  Ouch!
Fortunately, Robin was able to recover the game this time.  Then, with
5 hours left before the tournament was over, I screwed the pooch.  I
was fully kitted out and had just used the magic portal to go after
Rodney, when I picked up a wand of speed.  I went to break the wand, because
I didn't want to carry it and I didn't want anyone else to use it.  So,
I applied the want, it asked me whether I really wanted to break my wand
of polymorph, and I said yes.  Wait, wand of polymorph?  Argh.  There
went my +5 fireproof robe, my +5 fireproof T-Shirt, my +7 siver saber
(now an arrow), my +5 fireproof helm of brilliance (now a scale mail),
my +5 gauntlets of dexterity (now some other random piece of crap armor),
and my +4 fireproof speed boots.  Oops.  On the positive side, I still
had my gray dragon scale mail and my rustproof +7 fire brand.  Also,
on the positive side, I still hadn't woken Rodney yet.  On the negative
side, no markers and I'd already used up my WoW.  Oh well, time to
break my polyless conduct.  Spent a half hour scavenging magic armor,
got back to the castle, and started zapping my random scrolls and armor.
I ended up replacing my helm of brilliance and my T-Shirt.  I killed
a priest for a new robe, and I had water walking boots in my bag of
holding.  Got some polyed scrolls of enchant armor and enchant weapon,
so replaced my silver saber.  Never did replace my gauntlets of dexterity,
but those weren't a huge loss.  Ended up going from -42AC before the
screw up to -17AC afterwards, back to -30AC after the polypile.  This
is less than I usually try to ascend with, but the clock was ticking,
so "what the hell."  Well, I managed to finish with a full 1:15 to
spare.  I guess it just goes to show that where there's life, there's
hope.  If you don't despair, you can ever recover from pretty major
disasters.



